  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A corner-to-corner baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. The fabric is made from a diagonal grid of small treble-cluster "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "c2c-square"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "squares"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Work starts at one corner and grows with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "increase-row"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "increase rows"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " until the piece is at its widest. Then the rows shrink back down to the opposite corner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each square takes about 30 seconds on a 4 mm hook in DK cotton. The grid runs at 45 degrees to the finished edge, giving the fabric a subtle diagonal texture. DK cotton at this gauge makes 30 squares across the widest row and 36 rows down the length, for a total of 1,080 squares. Total yardage is around 400 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "400 g (one or more colours)"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch counter or tally",
              "qty": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One c2c square = 2.5 x 2.5 cm with a 4 mm hook in DK cotton. Make 4 squares in a row and measure: the strip should be 10 cm. This is more accurate than a traditional swatch for c2c because the square size is the gauge unit."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "sl st: slip stitch (to connect squares in a row)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tr (UK) / dc (US): treble"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "c2c square: ch 6, work 3 tr into the 4th ch from hook (a miniature cluster)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One c2c square"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 6. Work 3 tr into the 4th chain from hook. This is one c2c square: one arch and three trebles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Increase phase, Rows 1 to 30"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1: Make 1 c2c square. (1 square wide.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2: Sl st up the side of the square just made to reach the top. Ch 6, work 3 tr into 4th ch from hook (new square made). Sl st down into the ch-6 arch of Row 1. Ch 6, work 3 tr into 4th ch from hook (second new square). (2 squares wide.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each increase row: add one square at the start and one at the end. Continue until Row 30 (30 squares across the diagonal). This is the widest row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Decrease phase, Rows 31 to 60"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "From Row 31 onward, do not add a new square at the start of each row. Sl st across the top of the edge square instead of chaining a new one. Continue adding one at the end of alternate rows until Row 60 (one square, the opposite corner)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Colour changes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join a new colour at the start of any row. Cut the old colour, leaving a 15 cm tail. Colour changes show on the diagonal, producing diagonal stripe effects."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work one round of dc (UK) around the outer edge: 2 dc into each tr on open edges, 1 dc into each sl st point. This smooths the stepped diagonal edge. Fasten off. Secure all tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees, gentle. Dry flat. Pin to the stated dimensions while damp if the edges shift."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For a pixel design, use two colours per row and swap mid-row to make a picture in the diagonal grid. Or try the corner-to-corner adult throw in aran-weight yarn for a much faster version."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}